WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.567
-Today is Friday,
and that's usually when I

00:00:02.567 --> 00:00:03.901
catch up
with some personal stuff.

00:00:03.901 --> 00:00:05.968
You know, I check my inbox,
return some emails

00:00:05.968 --> 00:00:08.000
and of course send out
thank you notes.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:09.701
And I was...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.701 --> 00:00:11.000
...running a bit behind today.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:12.267
So, I thought if you guys
wouldn't mind, I would like

00:00:12.267 --> 00:00:13.901
to write out my weekly
thank you notes right now.

00:00:13.901 --> 00:00:14.968
Is that okay with you?

00:00:14.968 --> 00:00:16.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.033 --> 00:00:17.801
Thank you.

00:00:17.801 --> 00:00:19.701
James -- James, can I get some
thank you note

00:00:19.701 --> 00:00:20.934
writing music, please?

00:00:20.934 --> 00:00:23.067
♪♪

00:00:23.067 --> 00:00:25.968
[ Laughter ]

00:00:25.968 --> 00:00:27.467
He was almost smiling
for a second.

00:00:27.467 --> 00:00:29.334
-A little bit.
-Almost.

00:00:29.334 --> 00:00:31.267
-And that's it.

00:00:31.267 --> 00:00:32.367
Wow.

00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:38.300
-Thank you, "Euphoria,"
for being the first show

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:40.567
whose parental warning is,
maybe just don't

00:00:40.567 --> 00:00:41.968
watch this with
your parents.

00:00:41.968 --> 00:00:44.000
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:45.300
[ Applause ]

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:47.067
Your show.
That's your show.

00:00:49.501 --> 00:00:50.834
-Have you seen it?
-What's that?

00:00:50.834 --> 00:00:52.067
-You watch "Euphoria"?

00:00:52.067 --> 00:00:53.400
-What's that?
-You watch "Euphoria"?

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:54.834
-Yeah, of course.
-It's a good show.

00:00:54.834 --> 00:00:56.834
-It's fantastic, yeah.
-It's for the kids, right?

00:00:56.834 --> 00:00:58.801
-I watch with my parents.
-Do you really?

00:00:58.801 --> 00:01:00.100
-No.

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:02.501
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.501 --> 00:01:03.868
I don't watch anything
with my parents.

00:01:03.868 --> 00:01:05.701
-No, it's embarrassing.
-Anything risque or anything.

00:01:05.701 --> 00:01:07.000
-Yeah, no.
-I'd be embarrassed.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.767
-I don't even like watching
risque stuff with myself.

00:01:08.767 --> 00:01:10.133
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.133 --> 00:01:13.200
I, like, close my own eyes,
go "Don't look." You know?

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:14.534
-You close your eyes
and you blind fold yourself?

00:01:14.534 --> 00:01:15.901
-Yeah, blindfold myself.
"Don't look."

00:01:15.901 --> 00:01:17.734
This is risque.

00:01:17.734 --> 00:01:19.067
-Well, it looks like you
left yourself a little crack --

00:01:19.067 --> 00:01:20.934
-Well, I let myself see
so I know what not to watch.

00:01:20.934 --> 00:01:22.334
-Oh, yeah, yes.

00:01:22.334 --> 00:01:25.667
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.667 --> 00:01:30.133
Thank you, the D.C. Trucker
convoy protesting vaccines

00:01:30.133 --> 00:01:31.934
for answering the question,
what would happen

00:01:31.934 --> 00:01:33.968
if Optimus Prime got really
into QAnon.

00:01:33.968 --> 00:01:36.267
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:42.567 --> 00:01:45.901
Thank you, February weather,
for giving me 28 chances

00:01:45.901 --> 00:01:48.033
to wear the wrong thing
every day.

00:01:48.033 --> 00:01:49.868
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:49.868 --> 00:01:51.067
Are you kidding me?

00:01:51.067 --> 00:01:52.200
70 degrees?

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:53.467
-I'm leaving my coat at home.

00:01:53.467 --> 00:01:55.067
-No, it's 30 degrees.
-30?

00:01:55.067 --> 00:01:56.267
-Yeah.

00:01:58.434 --> 00:02:02.167
Thank you, "Love Is Blind"
for reminding us that two people

00:02:02.167 --> 00:02:05.033
can fall in love as long
as they drink enough wine

00:02:05.033 --> 00:02:06.901
and never have to be in
the same room as each other.

00:02:06.901 --> 00:02:09.734
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.734 --> 00:02:11.901
[ Applause ]

00:02:15.801 --> 00:02:18.734
-Thank you, Kraft,
for calling new plant-based

00:02:18.734 --> 00:02:20.868
hot dogs "Not Hot Dogs."

00:02:20.868 --> 00:02:23.133
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.133 --> 00:02:24.968
Or as 7-Eleven, hot dogs put it,

00:02:24.968 --> 00:02:26.200
"Hey, that's our thing.

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:28.234
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:28.234 --> 00:02:31.300
It's a hot dog or a taquito.

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:32.968
Just take a bite.
You'll find out what it is.

00:02:32.968 --> 00:02:34.634
Oh, it's a taquito.
-Oh.

00:02:34.634 --> 00:02:35.968
I thought it was a hot dog.

00:02:35.968 --> 00:02:39.667
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.667 --> 00:02:42.434
-Thank you, the original
"Law &amp; Order" for coming back

00:02:42.434 --> 00:02:44.834
to TV after 12 long years.

00:02:44.834 --> 00:02:46.367
I really thought
that you were done-done.

00:02:46.367 --> 00:02:48.767
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.767 --> 00:02:51.200
[ Rim shot ]

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:52.968
[ Applause ]

00:02:55.901 --> 00:02:59.267
Thank you, buying corn tortillas
at the grocery store.

00:02:59.267 --> 00:03:02.367
I only need three or four, but
sure, I guess I'll take 600.

00:03:02.367 --> 00:03:04.167
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:04.167 --> 00:03:07.067
You want 600 tortillas?

00:03:07.067 --> 00:03:08.868
-They're all stuck together.

00:03:08.868 --> 00:03:10.667
They're one tortilla.

00:03:10.667 --> 00:03:12.367
[ Imitating tortilla ripping ]

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:19.534
-Thank you, wind, for just being
air that's in a hurry.

00:03:19.534 --> 00:03:21.634
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:23.901
[ Applause ]

00:03:23.901 --> 00:03:25.000
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:26.734
I got to -- I got to go.

00:03:26.734 --> 00:03:28.467
I got things to do,
I got things to do.

00:03:30.634 --> 00:03:33.767
Thank you, wine bottle opener,
for always looking like

00:03:33.767 --> 00:03:36.200
you desperately need
to shave your armpits.

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:37.267
There you have it,
right there, folks.

00:03:37.267 --> 00:03:38.267
Those are my thank you notes.

